(D8 — a zero width beside a precision is refused, though a zero width
 alone is a legal no-op (`{n:0}`, `{n:00}` print 63) and a width
 composes with a precision (`{n:1.2}` prints 63.00).
 Ran: /usr/bin/vox D8.vox -o p   (vox 0.4.16, VOX_CORE_PATH unset)
 expected output:
   error: '0.2' is not a format specifier Vox knows
   (compile error - no binary is produced)
)
a number called n is 63.
Print "[{n:0.2}]".
